Mudang Korean Shaman costume in progress, designed by @jaimesunwoo and her mother Clara Sunwoo with research advice from  @shaman.mudang

This custom design is inspired by Mudang regalia (see last image for our research reference). We decided on a simplified belt and sash and a lustrous hat with subtle floral touches.

Mudang Jenn, a practicing Korean American shaman in NYC, shared her knowledge with us. Here's what she had to say: "Mudangs wear many types of sinbok (spirit regalia) depending on the spirit they represent. Since the mudang character is wearing white cotton hanbok, then the best way to build on that is Chilseong regalia."

